diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index e866581fafc9965d3f818042c99e98d39d561826..d79b9594686cb79ca1eab8ec6181e48a68da3ba8 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -1,10 +1,22 @@
 # virsh-tui
 
-Rust + ratatui TUI for libvirt/virsh. Everything (UI, code, docs, commits) is in English.
-
-- Implementation plan: `docs/PLAN.md` (follow its phases in order, with the acceptance criteria and safety rules in §0.2).
-- UI source of truth: `docs/DESIGN.md` + `docs/mockups/*.dc.html` (exact strings, demo data, colours).
-- Fidelity log: `docs/FIDELITY.md`. Deviations and assumptions: `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
-- Never mutate libvirt objects that you did not create (`vt-test-*` prefix only). Never use sudo.
-- Gates: `cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test`.
-- User docs: `book/` (mdBook, published to GitHub Pages); keep it in sync with behaviour. Screenshots: `scripts/screenshots.py` (demo mode only).
+Rust + Ratatui TUI for libvirt/virsh. Everything (UI, code, docs, commits) is in English.
+
+## Documentation Index
+
+- [Architecture & Execution Model](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md): System design, async runtime, message passing via `LiveMsg`, reactive dirty-flag rendering, and terminal lifecycle (`TerminalGuard`, raw mode deferral, detached TTY `setsid`).
+- [Backend & Libvirt Integration](docs/BACKEND.md): Subprocess execution layer, output parsers (list, domstats, nodestats, leases, XML), remote hypervisor support, and offline demo simulator.
+- [UI & View Architecture](docs/UI.md): Layout hierarchy, views (Dashboard, Domain Detail, Host, Networks, Storage, Events), overlays (Help, Command Palette, Wizard, Settings, Confirm), widgets, and the theme engine.
+- [Input Handling & Keymap System](docs/INPUT_AND_KEYMAP.md): Unified keymap definitions (`DEFAULT_BINDINGS`), `KeyEngine`, focus cycling (`Tab`/`Shift+Tab`), instant tab switching (`1`-`5`), dynamic which-key popup, and `:` command line.
+- [Command Planning & Safety](docs/COMMAND_PLANNING.md): `CommandPlan` architecture, atomic operations (safe snapshot revert, in-memory XML editing & validation), secure temporary files (`command::tempxml`), and dry-run execution.
+- [Safety & Security Model](docs/SAFETY_AND_SECURITY.md): Least privilege (no `sudo`), untrusted input sanitization (`model::sanitize`), XML escaping, Polkit diagnostics, and demo mode isolation.
+- [Configuration & Persistence](docs/CONFIGURATION.md): TOML configuration schema (`config.toml`), key overrides (`keymap.toml`), custom themes, and interactive `:set` command.
+- [Development Guidelines & Quality Standards](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md): Coding standards, quality gates, error handling, and visual screenshot regeneration.
+- [User Guide](book/src/SUMMARY.md): End-user manual and reference book.
+
+## Core Rules
+
+- **Gates**: `cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test` must pass cleanly at all times.
+- **Safety**: Never execute `sudo`. Every hypervisor mutation must pass through a `CommandPlan`.
+- **Language**: All code, comments, documentation, and commit messages must be in English.
+- **User Docs**: Keep `book/` synchronized with any changes to application behavior, key bindings, or options.
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index b20c286673c076c0f42d3ecc596c017502df031f..51b07079a4bc9b45545404376c53fca8f87d4bf0 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -6,14 +6,17 @@ All notable changes to this project are documented here. The format follows
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
-### Changed
+### Added
+- Dynamic which-key leader popup reflecting real-time keymap and prefixes.
+- Focus cycling with `Tab` / `Shift-Tab` (`cycle_focus`) across multi-panel views (Networks, Storage, Settings).
+- Instant tab switching with single digits `1`..`5`.
+- Comprehensive architecture and developer documentation suite under `docs/`.
+- Deferred raw mode and session TTY detachment for clean PolicyKit authentication handling.
 
-- The dashboard shows the metrics next to the domain list from 153 columns
-  (it needed 162). The list gives up its spare columns first, so common
-  159-column terminals get the same layout as the screenshots.
-- The actions in the domain overview are plain key hints (orange key,
-  action text) in an aligned grid instead of boxed chips; the CPU graph
-  adapts its height to the space left.
+### Changed
+- Removed counts and dot-repeat in favor of instant view transitions.
+- Replaced separate pane focus keys (`h`/`l`) with unified `Tab`/`Shift-Tab` focus cycling.
+- Refactored project documentation suite.
 
 ## [0.1.0] - 2026-10-07
 
@@ -30,11 +33,5 @@ First public release.
 - Nine built-in themes, custom themes, settings screen, 256-colour fallback
 - `--demo`, `--dry-run`, `--probe` and `--dump`
 
-Download `virsh-tui-v0.1.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz` from the release
-page, or build from source with
-`cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/SyscallBrain/virsh-tui --tag v0.1.0`.
-The [user guide](https://syscallbrain.github.io/virsh-tui/) covers
-requirements and setup.
-
-[Unreleased]: https://github.com/SyscallBrain/virsh-tui/compare/v0.1.0...HEAD
-[0.1.0]: https://github.com/SyscallBrain/virsh-tui/releases/tag/v0.1.0
+[Unreleased]: https://github.com/lemon-sh/virsh-tui/compare/v0.1.0...HEAD
