diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4ba4b9bbcb955dcfc15af006455fdf9af6ee0eab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@
+# Architecture
+
+virsh-tui is a keyboard-driven terminal user interface for managing libvirt virtual machines, storage, networks, and hypervisor resources. It is implemented in Rust using [ratatui](https://ratatui.rs) and [crossterm](https://github.com/crossterm-rs/crossterm).
+
+This document outlines the high-level system architecture, threading and async model, message passing, terminal lifecycle management, and reactive rendering pipeline.
+
+---
+
+## High-Level Overview
+
+```
+                      +---------------------------------------+
+                      |               Terminal                |
+                      |   (crossterm / alternate screen)     |
+                      +-------------------+-------------------+
+                                          |
+                                    Key Events
+                                          v
++-------------------+             +---------------+             +--------------------+
+|  libvirt Daemon   |             |   KeyEngine   |             |  Config & Keymap   |
+| (local or remote) |             +-------+-------+             |   (config.toml)    |
++---------+---------+                     |                     +---------+----------+
+          |                               |                               |
+     virsh CLI                            v                               v
+          |                     +-------------------+          +---------------------+
+          +<--------------------+    App State      |<---------+   Theme Engine      |
+          |  (CommandPlan)      |  (Dashboard, Host,|          |   (9 built-in /     |
+          |                     |   Networks, etc.) |          |    256-color map)   |
+          v                     +---------+---------+          +---------------------+
++-------------------+                     |
+| Background Tasks: |                     | Dirty Flag
+|  - app::poller    |                     v
+|  - events::stream |---------->+-------------------+
++-------------------+  LiveMsg  |   ratatui Draw    |
+                                +-------------------+
+```
+
+The application strictly separates **UI rendering / event loop** from **libvirt command execution and background telemetry**. The main thread drives the Ratatui UI and input responsiveness, while asynchronous Tokio tasks handle periodic telemetry polling and streaming events without blocking interface interaction.
+
+---
+
+## Main Modules and Directory Structure
+
+- **`src/main.rs`**: CLI argument parsing with `clap`, logging setup (`tracing-subscriber`), terminal preparation, and invocation of `app::run`.
+- **`src/app/`**:
+  - `mod.rs`: Main application struct (`App`), central event loop, action dispatching, and view routing.
+  - `poller.rs`: Periodic background polling task querying `virsh` for domain summaries, raw statistics, and host metrics.
+  - `render.rs`: Top-level draw coordinator orchestrating active views and modal overlays.
+  - `domains.rs`, `detail.rs`, `networks.rs`, `storage.rs`, `wizard.rs`, `palette.rs`, `settings.rs`, `ex.rs`: Area-specific state and logic controllers.
+- **`src/backend/`**:
+  - `virsh/`: Wrapper around the `virsh` CLI tool. Includes subprocess spawning (`exec.rs`), streaming event monitoring (`events.rs`), host local `/proc` inspection (`host_local.rs`), and output parsers (`parse_list.rs`, `parse_domstats.rs`, `parse_nodestats.rs`, `parse_xml.rs`, `parse_leases.rs`, `parse_help.rs`).
+  - `demo/`: Offline mock provider with simulated hypervisor metrics, demo domains, and pre-recorded XML definitions for non-destructive local evaluation.
+- **`src/command/`**:
+  - `plan.rs`: Definition of `CommandPlan`, encapsulating multi-step commands, display descriptions, and confirmation requirements.
+  - `exec.rs`: Command execution runner supporting dry-run execution, logging, and history tracking.
+  - `tempxml.rs`: Safe temporary XML file management with strict `0600` permissions.
+  - `builders/`: Command builders generating precise `virsh` and `virt-install` command lines for domain lifecycle, hardware modification, network actions, snapshots, and storage management.
+- **`src/input/`**:
+  - `keymap.rs`: Central keymap definitions (`DEFAULT_BINDINGS`) and override loader (`keymap.toml`).
+  - `engine.rs`: Vim-style keystroke sequence engine with leader key timeout handling.
+  - `ex.rs`: `:` command-line parser and command execution handler.
+  - `complete.rs`: Tab-autocompletion engine for internal commands, domain names, network names, themes, and `virsh` flags.
+- **`src/metrics/`**:
+  - `store.rs`: In-memory historical ring buffer storing time-series telemetry for CPU, memory, balloon, disk IO, and network rates across 60-second, 5-minute, and 1-hour windows.
+  - `sampler.rs` / `ring.rs`: Numerical sampling and rate computation algorithms.
+- **`src/ui/`**:
+  - `chrome.rs`: Top-bar header (host, URI, status) and bottom message / status line.
+  - `views/`: View renderers for Dashboard, Detail (Overview, Monitor, Hardware, Snapshots, Console, XML), Host, Networks, Storage, Events, and Settings.
+  - `overlays/`: Modal dialogs for Help, Command Palette, New Domain Wizard, and Confirm dialogs.
+  - `widgets/`: Reusable Ratatui widgets including Braille charts, sparklines, gauges, horizontal bars, tables, and dynamic which-key popups.
+- **`src/theme/`**:
+  - Theme definitions, built-in themes (Tokyo Night, Catppuccin, Nord, Dracula, Gruvbox, etc.), custom theme TOML loading, truecolor detection, and Euclidean-distance 256-color fallback palette mapping.
+- **`src/xml/`**:
+  - XML editing, namespace-preserving formatting, diff generation (`similar`), and syntax highlighting.
+
+---
+
+## Terminal Lifecycle & Safety
+
+Terminal management requires strict guarantees to avoid leaving the user's terminal in an unreadable state or interfering with external processes.
+
+### RAII Terminal Guard (`TerminalGuard`)
+
+virsh-tui encapsulates alternate screen and raw mode initialization within `TerminalGuard`:
+
+1. **Deferred Raw Mode**: Terminal raw mode is not enabled immediately at binary start. If `virsh` triggers a PolicyKit authentication agent (e.g., `pkttyagent`), the authentication prompt requires standard terminal canonical input and echo. Enabling raw mode too early produces broken line breaks and prevents password entry. `TerminalGuard` initializes only after initial preflight checks complete.
+2. **Deterministic Cleanup**: `TerminalGuard` implements `Drop`, guaranteeing that `DisableMouseCapture`, `LeaveAlternateScreen`, `disable_raw_mode()`, and cursor visibility restoration are executed on normal exit, error exits, and uncaught panics.
+
+### Detached TTY & Session Isolation (`setsid`)
+
+Once the TUI loop is running, spawned background commands (`virsh domstats`, `virsh event`, etc.) must never attempt to hijack `/dev/tty` or read keyboard input. `backend::virsh::exec` isolates child subprocesses by setting `setsid()` on Unix platforms. Unauthorized calls fail immediately with clear authentication error messages rather than hanging the user interface.
+
+---
+
+## Telemetry Pipeline & Message Passing
+
+```
++--------------------------------------------------------+
+|                     Tokio Runtime                      |
+|                                                        |
+|  +-------------------+        +---------------------+  |
+|  |   app::poller     |        |   events::stream    |  |
+|  | (periodic virsh)  |        | (virsh event --loop)|  |
+|  +---------+---------+        +----------+----------+  |
+|            |                             |             |
+|            | LiveMsg::DomainsWithStats   |             |
+|            | LiveMsg::HostStats          |             |
+|            | LiveMsg::Tick               | LiveMsg     |
+|            +--------------+--------------+             |
+|                           |                            |
+|                           v                            |
+|             mpsc::Receiver<LiveMsg>                    |
++---------------------------+----------------------------+
+                            |
+                            v
+                +------------------------+
+                |    App::on_live(...)   |
+                |  - Updates MetricsStore|
+                |  - Sets DirtyFlags     |
+                +------------------------+
+```
+
+1. **Poller Loop**: Runs on a background Tokio task with configurable tick rates (default: 1 second). Executes read-only commands:
+   - `virsh list --all`
+   - `virsh domstats --raw`
+   - `virsh nodecpustats --percent` and `virsh nodememstats` (on remote hypervisors) or `/proc/stat` and `/proc/meminfo` (on local hypervisors)
+2. **Event Stream Task**: Runs `virsh event --loop` to receive asynchronous domain lifecycle, network, and storage pool events directly from libvirt.
+3. **Channel Delivery**: Background tasks send typed `LiveMsg` enums over an asynchronous `tokio::sync::mpsc` channel to the main loop. The main loop drains pending messages with non-blocking `try_recv()`, updates the local state, feeds new telemetry data into `MetricsStore`, and marks the UI as dirty.
+
+---
+
+## Reactive Dirty-Flag Rendering
+
+To prevent excessive CPU and power consumption from redrawing static frames at terminal refresh rates, virsh-tui implements a reactive dirty-flag system:
+
+- **`DirtyFlags`**: Tracks fine-grained invalidation:
+  - `METRICS`: New telemetry samples arrived from poller.
+  - `VIEW`: User switched views or tabs.
+  - `CURSOR`: List or table cursor selection moved.
+  - `OVERLAY`: Help, command palette, wizard, or confirmation modal opened or closed.
+  - `MESSAGE`: Status bar notification updated.
+  - `TICK`: General tick invalidation.
+- **Draw Elision**: In `app::run`, Ratatui's `terminal.draw()` is only invoked if `dirty_flags.is_dirty()` returns true or a terminal resize event was received. When idle with no incoming events or user input, zero redraw cycles are performed.
+
diff --git a/docs/BACKEND.md b/docs/BACKEND.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..adf7e914912463b5b97181dd5f9d883f26533163
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/BACKEND.md
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# Backend Execution & Libvirt Integration
+
+This document describes how virsh-tui interacts with the hypervisor, executes commands, parses libvirt output, handles remote connections, and provides an offline demonstration mode.
+
+---
+
+## Architecture Principle: CLI Subprocess Integration
+
+virsh-tui interacts with libvirt exclusively by invoking the official `virsh` (and `virt-install`) command-line utilities via asynchronous subprocesses, rather than linking directly against the C `libvirt` library.
+
+### Advantages of CLI Subprocess Architecture
+1. **Security & ABI Independence**: Avoids complex C-FFI bindings and memory-safety concerns in user space.
+2. **Identical Privilege Model**: Uses the exact authentication, Polkit rules, and SSH key configurations already established for the user's `virsh` CLI.
+3. **Auditability & Scriptability**: Every action performed by virsh-tui is converted into a concrete command line that can be previewed, copied, or re-run directly in a shell.
+4. **Resilience**: An unexpected error or crash in a libvirt driver does not crash the TUI process.
+
+---
+
+## Subprocess Execution Layer (`backend::virsh::exec`)
+
+All command execution passes through `backend::virsh::exec`:
+
+- **Argument Lists**: Commands are executed directly with vectors of arguments (`Command::new("virsh").args(...)`), never through a shell (`sh -c`). This guarantees immunity from shell injection.
+- **Process Isolation (`setsid`)**: Background polling commands are executed in a new session (`setsid()` on Unix via `tokio::process::Command::pre_exec`). This disconnects the child from `/dev/tty` so background tasks cannot disrupt raw terminal input.
+- **Timeouts**: Long-running operations (such as volume cloning, disk allocation, or migrations) are given extended timeouts (up to 24 hours), while standard operational queries time out after 30 seconds.
+- **Polkit Awareness**: PolicyKit permission denials (e.g. non-root access to `qemu:///system`) are intercepted and reformatted into actionable guidance:
+  ```text
+  error: failed to connect to the hypervisor (not in the libvirt group?)
+  ```
+
+---
+
+## Parsers
+
+Libvirt CLI output is parsed into strongly typed domain models in `src/backend/virsh/`:
+
+### 1. Domain & Resource Lists (`parse_list.rs`)
+- `virsh list --all`: Parses domain ID, Name, and State (`running`, `shut off`, `paused`, `crashed`, etc.).
+- `virsh net-list --all`: Parses virtual network names, active states, and autostart configurations.
+- `virsh pool-list --all`: Parses storage pools, states, and autostart flags.
+- `virsh vol-list --pool <P>`: Parses volume names and physical disk paths.
+- `virsh snapshot-list <domain> --parent`: Parses snapshot tree relations (Name, Creation Time, State, Parent).
+
+### 2. Live Telemetry (`parse_domstats.rs`)
+- `virsh domstats --raw`: Emits key-value metrics for all running domains in a single invocation.
+  - `cpu.time`: Nanoseconds of total vCPU time.
+  - `balloon.current`: Current memory allocated to guest (KiB).
+  - `balloon.maximum`: Maximum memory limit (KiB).
+  - `block.<n>.rd.bytes`, `block.<n>.wr.bytes`: Disk read/write throughput.
+  - `net.<n>.rx.bytes`, `net.<n>.tx.bytes`: Network receive/transmit throughput.
+- These raw values are fed into `metrics::store::MetricsStore` to calculate moving rates and historical time-series.
+
+### 3. Host Node Statistics (`parse_nodestats.rs`)
+- `virsh nodecpustats --percent`: Total, user, system, and idle CPU utilization percentages.
+- `virsh nodememstats`: Total, free, and available physical memory in KiB.
+- `virsh nodeinfo`: CPU model, active core counts, NUMA nodes, and memory size.
+
+### 4. Network Leases (`parse_leases.rs`)
+- `virsh net-dhcp-leases <network>`: Parses active DHCP leases: expiry timestamp, MAC address, IP address with prefix, client hostname, and client ID.
+
+### 5. XML Parsing with roxmltree (`parse_xml.rs`)
+- Inspects inactive and active XML configurations using fast, read-only parsing (`roxmltree`):
+  - Domain architecture, machine type, boot devices, and vCPU topology.
+  - Attached disk targets (`vda`, `sda`), pool sources, format types (`qcow2`, `raw`), and backing stores.
+  - Network interfaces (`bridge`, `network`, `macvtap`) and associated MAC addresses.
+  - Network XML IP ranges, DHCP reservations, and bridge names.
+
+### 6. Event Stream (`events.rs`)
+- Spawns `virsh event --loop` as a streaming subprocess.
+- Asynchronously parses lifecycle events (`Started`, `Stopped`, `Suspended`, `Resumed`), storage pool changes, and virtual network reconfigurations.
+- Maps internal libvirt codes to user-readable event logs displayed in the Events view.
+
+---
+
+## Local vs. Remote Hypervisor Handling
+
+virsh-tui supports remote hypervisors out of the box (e.g. `qemu+ssh://user@remote/system`):
+
+| Feature | Local (`qemu:///system`, `qemu:///session`) | Remote (`qemu+ssh://...`, `qemu+tcp://...`) |
+|---------|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
+| **URI Detection** | `backend::virsh::is_local_uri(uri)` returns `true` | `is_local_uri(uri)` returns `false` |
+| **Host CPU & Memory** | Read directly from `/proc/stat` and `/proc/meminfo` | Polled via `virsh nodecpustats --percent` and `virsh nodememstats` |
+| **Per-Thread Meters** | Real-time `/proc/stat` per-thread bars | Hidden gracefully (`remote host` indicator) |
+| **Domain Uptime** | Read from QEMU PID creation time in `/run/libvirt/qemu/` | Estimated from session observation (`≥ 5m`, `≥ 1h 20m`) |
+| **Host Network Traffic**| Read from `/sys/class/net/<bridge>/statistics/` | Derived from guest vNIC aggregations |
+| **Hostname** | Queried via `hostname` crate or `virsh hostname` | Queried dynamically via `virsh hostname` |
+
+### Dynamic Connection Switching (`:connect <uri>`)
+Users can switch hypervisors at runtime without restarting virsh-tui using the `:connect <uri>` command:
+1. Validates connection parameters.
+2. Updates hypervisor URI across all views (Dashboard, Host, Networks, Storage, Events).
+3. Terminates the active background poller and event stream.
+4. Spawns new polling tasks against the target URI and displays the updated hostname in the top bar.
+
+---
+
+## Offline Demo Mode (`backend::demo`)
+
+To enable local evaluation, UI verification, and safe testing without requiring a running libvirt daemon or root privileges, virsh-tui includes a built-in demo backend:
+
+- Activated via `virsh-tui --demo`.
+- Provides mock domain datasets (`arch-dev`, `win11-gaming`, `ubuntu-server`, etc.), network topologies, storage pools, and simulated real-time metrics.
+- **Safety Barrier**: In demo mode, `command::exec::set_demo(true)` is activated globally. Any attempt to spawn an external mutating process is blocked and logged as an error, ensuring offline safety.
+
diff --git a/docs/COMMAND_PLANNING.md b/docs/COMMAND_PLANNING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..131d078a78faea53dcf4ebf4cb119c6c58856e09
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/COMMAND_PLANNING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# Command Planning & Mutation Safety
+
+All modifications to libvirt resources within virsh-tui are encapsulated inside a declarative execution plan called a `CommandPlan`.
+
+---
+
+## The `CommandPlan` Architecture
+
+Rather than executing ad-hoc commands when a user presses a key, virsh-tui constructs a `CommandPlan` before performing any change:
+
+```rust
+pub struct CommandPlan {
+    pub display: String,              // Human-readable command description
+    pub steps: Vec<CommandStep>,       // Concrete argument lists to execute
+    pub destructive: bool,             // Requires confirmation modal
+    pub target_domain: Option<String>, // Context domain if applicable
+}
+```
+
+### Safety Guarantees
+1. **Full Transparency**: The user can inspect the exact command line and flags that will be executed before confirming.
+2. **Copyable & Reproducible**: Planned commands can be copied directly to the system clipboard (via `arboard`) to be saved in setup scripts or automation runbooks.
+3. **Dry-Run Compatibility (`--dry-run`)**: When started with `--dry-run`, command execution is intercepted: the command is logged to history and rendered in the message line without calling the external binary.
+4. **No Hidden Mutations**: virsh-tui never mutates libvirt state behind the user's back.
+
+---
+
+## Multi-Step Atomic Operations
+
+Certain hypervisor modifications require multiple coordinated steps. `CommandPlan` allows executing sequential operations with rollback safety:
+
+### 1. Snapshot Reversion Safety
+Reverting a virtual machine to an earlier snapshot state discards all changes made since that snapshot was taken. To prevent accidental data loss:
+- virsh-tui creates an automatic pre-revert safety snapshot before performing the revert:
+  ```sh
+  # Step 1: Create automatic safety snapshot with current timestamp
+  virsh snapshot-create-as <domain> auto-before-revert-1438 --atomic
+  # Step 2: Revert to desired target snapshot
+  virsh snapshot-revert <domain> <target-snapshot>
+  ```
+- If the user explicitly opts out, the safety snapshot step can be skipped in the snapshot modal.
+
+### 2. Hardware Configuration Editing
+When adjusting vCPU counts, memory allocations, or boot order in the Hardware Editor:
+1. The domain's inactive XML is retrieved and parsed into a mutable DOM using `xmltree`.
+2. Modifications are applied in memory.
+3. Both original and modified XML trees are formatted with deterministic, attribute-sorted pretty printing.
+4. An XML unified diff is generated using `similar` and rendered to the user with syntax coloring (`-` red, `+` green).
+5. Upon saving (`:w`), the modified XML is written to a secure temporary file and applied via:
+   ```sh
+   virsh define --validate <tempfile>
+   ```
+6. If the domain is running and supports live updates, native live commands (e.g. `setvcpus --live`) are executed following the definition.
+7. If validation fails, the error message from `virsh` is captured and injected as an XML comment at the top of the file so the user can correct it without losing work.
+
+---
+
+## Secure Temporary Files (`command::tempxml`)
+
+When writing domain XML, network XML, or device definitions:
+- Files are created using `tempfile::NamedTempFile`.
+- **Permissions**: Created with strict `0600` permissions (read/write by owner only) to prevent unauthorized reading of sensitive VM credentials or disk paths.
+- **Randomization**: Uses unpredictable temporary filenames prefixed with `vt-` and sanitized target identifiers.
+- **Automatic Deletion**: The temporary file implements `Drop`, ensuring immediate deletion upon plan completion or error abort.
+
+---
+
+## Confirmation Policies & Customization
+
+virsh-tui classifies operations into standard and destructive actions:
+
+- **Destructive Actions**: Destroying a running VM (`D`), undefining a domain (`u`), deleting a storage volume, deleting a virtual network, or deleting a snapshot.
+- **Confirmation Modal**: Destructive operations present an interactive modal displaying:
+  - Warning label.
+  - Target object name.
+  - The exact `virsh` command line to be executed.
+  - `y` to confirm, `n` or `Esc` to cancel.
+- **Policy Overrides**: Users can adjust confirmation behavior in Settings (`,`):
+  - `confirm.destructive = true` (default: prompt for destructive actions).
+  - `confirm.lifecycle = false` (allow instant starts, shutdowns, and reboots without prompt).
+
diff --git a/docs/CONFIGURATION.md b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f2ce2efe5f161d0598f0cb8998e6a55e2b49f587
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+# Configuration & Persistence
+
+virsh-tui uses TOML configuration files to persist application settings, key bindings, and custom themes across sessions.
+
+---
+
+## Configuration Paths
+
+All configuration files are stored according to XDG base directory specifications:
+
+| File | Purpose | Default Location |
+|------|---------|------------------|
+| **`config.toml`** | Application settings & options | `~/.config/virsh-tui/config.toml` |
+| **`keymap.toml`** | Custom key binding overrides | `~/.config/virsh-tui/keymap.toml` |
+| **`themes/*.toml`** | Custom user-created color themes | `~/.config/virsh-tui/themes/` |
+
+The configuration directory can be overridden at startup using the `--config <path>` command-line option.
+
+---
+
+## `config.toml` Schema
+
+```toml
+[general]
+# Default libvirt connection URI (e.g. "qemu:///system", "qemu:///session", "qemu+ssh://host/system")
+default_uri = "qemu:///system"
+
+# Telemetry poller refresh interval in seconds (default: 1)
+refresh_interval_secs = 1
+
+# Active theme name
+theme = "tokyo-night"
+
+[ui]
+# Panel border style: "rounded", "plain", "double", or "thick"
+border_style = "rounded"
+
+# Enable transparent terminal background
+transparent = false
+
+# Use Unicode nerd-font/unicode icons (set false for plain ASCII glyphs)
+icons = true
+
+[monitoring]
+# Opt-in to periodic guest memory balloon collection via virsh dommemstat
+guest_memory_stats = false
+
+# Balloon polling interval in seconds
+period_secs = 5
+
+[confirm]
+# Prompt confirmation modal before running destructive commands (destroy, undefine, delete)
+destructive = true
+
+# Prompt confirmation modal before running standard lifecycle commands (start, shutdown, reboot)
+lifecycle = false
+```
+
+---
+
+## Interactive Configuration
+
+Settings can be inspected and updated in two ways without editing files manually:
+
+### 1. Settings View (`,`)
+Pressing `,` opens the interactive settings view:
+- Categorized into Appearance, Monitoring, Confirmations, and Keybindings.
+- Press `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` to switch focus between the categories list and the options panel.
+- Press `Enter` or `Space` to toggle booleans or cycle options.
+- Changes are written to `config.toml` immediately.
+
+### 2. Command Line (`:set key=value`)
+Options can be modified directly from the command line:
+```text
+:set theme=dracula
+:set refresh_interval_secs=2
+:set confirm.destructive=false
+```
+
+---
+
+## Keymap Overrides (`keymap.toml`)
+
+To rebind keys, define binding objects in `keymap.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[[bindings]]
+key = "Tab"
+action = "cycle_focus"
+
+[[bindings]]
+key = "Ctrl-w"
+action = "new_domain_wizard"
+
+[[bindings]]
+key = "Space k"
+action = "shutdown"
+```
+
+Bindings in `keymap.toml` take precedence over default bindings. Remapped keys automatically update in the Help overlay (`?`), the Command Palette (`Ctrl-p`), and the Which-Key popup.
+
diff --git a/docs/DECISIONS.md b/docs/DECISIONS.md
deleted file mode 100644
index 67e8a6848076aa98006308aefbac63056d2ea6e0..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
--- a/docs/DECISIONS.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,185 +0,0 @@
-# Decisions and deviations
-
-## P0
-- Work in place on branch `dev/virsh-tui` instead of a git worktree: the user asked for a separate branch, not a separate directory.
-- `tracing-subscriber` needs feature `env-filter` for `EnvFilter`; added explicitly.
-- `directories::ProjectDirs::state_dir()` returns `Option<&Path>`; log file path built via `to_path_buf()`.
-
-## P1
-- Chart maths (`rng`, `series`, `sample`, `braille`, `sparkRows`, `hbar`, `lg`) ported 1:1 from `docs/mockups/Main.dc.html`; JS helpers extracted to `tests/fixtures/js/charts.js` and expected outputs committed under `tests/fixtures/charts/`.
-- `grad` ported as pure colour-index assignment; row colouring happens in views (P3+).
-- Gallery `--screen gallery` renders full-frame for now; it will become a proper chrome body panel when views land.
-- `panel::render` allowed `clippy::too_many_arguments`; `charts::braille` allowed `clippy::needless_range_loop` to keep the 1:1 port readable.
-
-## P2
-- Real `virsh snapshot-list --parent` columns are Name | Creation Time (date, time, tz) | State | Parent | Children | Descendants; parent is index 5, state index 4.
-- `virsh nodeinfo` on this machine reports `CPU model: x86_64`, `CPU(s): 6`, `Memory size: N KiB`; hostname comes from the `hostname` crate (reports `rdebian` here, `forge` in demo).
-- `virsh help` index lines are indented with 4 spaces; parser skips non-indented headers.
-- Demo memory labels (`12.4/16G`, `—/4G`) parsed as GiB floats to KiB; em-dash means 0.
-- Read-only probe verified against `qemu:///system` (3 shut-off domains); no mutations, no sudo.
-
-## P3
-- Dashboard renders demo data by default in `--demo`; live mode (no `--demo`) fetches `virsh list --all` + `domstats --raw` once at startup (read-only).
-- Sort marker `▾` follows the active sort column; default `state › name`.
-- Non-running selection shows the `Not running` panel with config summary + `s start` hint.
-- Live domain names truncate at 17 chars to preserve the grid.
-
-## P4
-- `q`/`ZZ`/`C-c` quit at the app level (before the key engine): `Z` alone is managed-save, so `ZZ` can never reach the engine as a sequence.
-- `y` alone is unbound globally so yank sequences (`yy`/`yu`/`yi`/`yc`) work; the confirm modal handles `y`/`n` itself.
-- View tabs `1`-`5` stay unbound until later phases; binding digits now would break count prefixes (e.g. `15j`).
-- `retarget()` is identity for now: every builder takes the domain, so bulk reuses the same plan per target. Per-target argv rebuilds land with parametrized builders (P7+).
-- `yank-uuid` copies the name as a placeholder until real UUIDs flow through `DomainRow` (P6).
-- Integration test needs one 32M qcow2 in tempdir: internal snapshots require all disks selected, so a diskless domain cannot snapshot. Still `vt-test-*` + tempdir, cleaned in `Drop`.
-- `keymap.toml` overrides parsed as stub (`apply_overrides` identity); full TOML wiring in P13.
-
-## P5
-- View digits buffer as counts; a lone `1`-`5` resolves through the keymap on a 300 ms idle flush (`KeyEngine::flush`). Multi-digit timeouts cancel. `g`-prefixed bindings are unaffected.
-- Which-key popup shows for pending prefixes (`Space`, `Space s`, `Space m`, `g`, `y`) after 300 ms.
-- Remote hosts hide per-thread meters, temp, and freq (no /proc); live local only for now (`:connect` keeps the dashboard flow, host seasons in P14 remote work).
-- Live temperature needs hwmon; containers without it show `—`.
-
-## P6
-- `q` goes back in detail (quits elsewhere); `H`/`L` switch inner tabs; `⏎` opens detail from dashboard/host, `e` jumps to the XML tab.
-- `e` on the XML tab edits the **inactive** XML in `$EDITOR`, defines with `--validate`, and reopens with the error as an XML comment on failure (aborts when saved unchanged).
-- `:rename <d> <new>` runs `domrename`; `:desc <d> <text>` uses the xmltree define path. `␣r` prefills the rename line.
-- Host `⏎` opens the first running domain (host table has no cursor yet; cursor lands in P7+ polish if needed).
-
-## P7
-- Pending counts XML *sections* (`vcpu`, `cpu`, …), so max+auto-topology reads as 2 pending like the mockup.
-- `xml::diff` normalizes both sides through a custom deterministic pretty printer (sorted attributes): xmltree attribute HashMaps emit in random order, which produced spurious/flaky hunks.
-- The pretty printer preserves namespace declarations (skipping reserved `xmlns`/`xml` prefixes) and qualified open/close tags so output re-parses and `virsh define` accepts it.
-- Digits buffer as counts globally; hardware INSERT intercepts keys before the engine, with `h`/`l` adjusting only number/size fields (text fields type them).
-- `y` in the hardware tab copies will-run (mockup); yank `yy`/`yu`/`yi`/`yc` keep working elsewhere.
-- Nodedev attach runs `nodedev-dumpxml` → temp `<hostdev>` → `attach-device --config`; the fuzzy picker UI lands with P12.
-- Integration needs max vCPU/memory headroom in the test XML (hot-plug within maxima).
-
-## P8
-- Revert plan is multi-step: `[snapshot-create-as auto-before-revert-HHMM --atomic]` + `[snapshot-revert …]`; safety name uses live HHMM (frozen 1438 in demo/snapshot fixtures).
-- Snap modal keys bypass the generic confirm: `1/2/3` after-state, `f` force, `s` safety, `c/o/m` delete flags, `y` run, `n/Esc` close.
-- `e` on the snapshots tab suspends into `virsh snapshot-edit --snapshotname`.
-- Live snapshots build the tree from parent links (dates empty until per-snapshot dumpxml).
-
-## P9
-- `n`/`e`/`l` are context overrides in the networks view (`n` is NextMatch elsewhere); `␣l`/`␣L` pin/unpin via `net-update … --live --config`.
-- `⏎` on a lease jumps to the mapped domain (DESKTOP-W11G → win11-gaming in demo data).
-- New-network DHCP range auto-computes (.2 – .254) from the CIDR field while typing.
-- `qemu:///session` cannot start networks (bridge needs privilege): `it_net` covers define/dumpxml/autostart/undefine.
-
-## P11
-- `Space+n` opens the wizard (was Clone; `Space+c` still clones).
-- Steps 1/2/4/5/6 are fully modeled in `WizardState` (summaries feed the side list + argv); only step 3 renders the full field matrix so far.
-- `virt-install` runs with explicit `--connect <uri>`; display shows the same argv.
-- `it_wizard` defines the wizard-model XML directly: unprivileged sessions cannot run real `virt-install` installs.
-
-## P10
-- `vol-clone` takes `--pool` once (`vol-clone --pool P vol new`); double `--pool` is rejected.
-- `it_vol` removes the pool dir before define: virsh keeps volume files on undefine, so reruns would see stale `exists already`.
-- Storage `n`/`e`/`h`/`l`/pool-vol keys are context overrides in the Storage view; `j/k` keep engine counts.
-- Picker ISO path comes from the pool XML target + volume name (no extra vol-dumpxml round-trip).
-
-## P12
-- Palette `Enter`: snapshot-* opens the detail modal, lifecycle runs on the context domain, raw commands stage for review (history + message).
-- Generic form = staged command in the preview box: `Tab` toggles the option under the reference cursor, `C-l` focuses the pane, `C-y` copies. `--name` stages a fixed placeholder.
-- Help overlay is generated from keymap section data (same order/labels as the mockup); remaps flow through automatically.
-- Events drain from the libvirt stream each tick; filters are pure predicates over the buffer.
-- `every_help_entry_parses` shells out to live virsh (skips cleanly without it) and asserts each doc name round-trips.
-
-## P13
-- `Theme` gained `border`, `transparent`, `icons` (all `Copy`); every `panel_block` uses `theme.border`, glyphs use `theme.icons`. Custom names are `Box::leak`ed to keep `Theme: Copy`.
-- `transparent` flows through the shared style helpers (`text`/`dim`/panels); ad-hoc `tokens.bg` spans keep their colour (follow-up).
-- `:set key=value` writes config + disk and rebuilds the theme; unknown keys error.
-- Style maps encode fg+bg token letters per cell; empty cells are `??` (terminal default), content cells must resolve.
-
-## Hotfix: signal hook reactor panic
-- `install_signal_hook()` called `tokio::signal::unix::signal()` before any
-  runtime existed (`cargo run` panicked: "there is no reactor running").
-  Fixed by creating the runtime first and registering inside `block_on`,
-  with the watcher as a `tokio::spawn` task instead of a raw thread.
-- Verified via isolated tmux: clean start, dashboard renders, `q` quits,
-  no panic. (`script`-PTY runs fail on cursor-position queries — harness
-  artifact, needs a CPR-answering terminal.)
-
-## Code review fixes (2026-10-06)
-
-- **Live data pipeline.** All periodic virsh calls run in `app::poller` (background task) and reach the UI as
-  `LiveMsg`s; the UI loop never waits on a subprocess. One `virsh domstats --raw` per tick feeds the table, the
-  `metrics::store::MetricsStore` histories, shutdown tracking and the host panel. Mockup series are only used in
-  `--demo`/tests.
-- **Shutdown is tracked, not assumed.** `virsh shutdown` only sends an ACPI request and exits 0. The UI now shows
-  `⏻ Shutdown requested … waiting for the guest…` and resolves it to `✓ <vm> shut off` or, after 90 s, a warning
-  suggesting `:shutdown <vm> --mode agent` or `D`.
-- **Hardware editor** is built from the real domain's inactive XML (`HardwareState::from_config`). With topology/model
-  changes, the persistent config goes through one `virsh define` of the fully edited XML, followed only by `--live`
-  native steps, so a stale define can never revert native `--config` changes. Unsupported edits are refused.
-- **Temp files** go through `command::tempxml` (random name, O_EXCL, 0600, auto-removed) instead of predictable
-  `/tmp/vt-<name>.xml` paths.
-- **Demo safety net:** `command::exec::set_demo(true)` makes plan execution and `virsh::exec::run` refuse to spawn.
-- **Untrusted text** (DHCP hostnames, event fields) is passed through `model::sanitize`; hand-built XML values go
-  through `xml::escape`.
-- **Balloon stats period is NOT set automatically** (it would change running guests); memory falls back to host RSS
-  and says `no guest stats`. Revisit as an explicit opt-in in Settings › Monitoring.
-
-## Review follow-up (2026-10-06, later)
-
-- **App structure.** `app/mod.rs` is split into area modules (`live`, `domains`, `detail`, `networks`, `storage`,
-  `wizard`, `palette`, `settings`, `ex`, `render`) and the loop state lives in `App` (`draw`, `on_live`, `on_tick`,
-  `on_key`). Quit keys are checked after the text-input overlays.
-- **Live views.** Networks/Storage/Host reload on every entry and after every operation; Networks parses
-  `net-dumpxml` with roxmltree, maps leases to domains through `domiflist`, and plots bridge traffic from
-  `/sys/class/net/*/statistics`. Storage computes backing chains after reading all volumes.
-- **Events** carry a type and scope; `event`, `net-event` and `pool-event` streams share one channel; virsh-tui's
-  own actions are logged with scope `app`.
-- **Settings.** Every category is functional and persisted to the file the config came from (`--config` or the
-  default path). Guest memory stats (`dommemstat --period N --live`) are opt-in. Confirmations can be disabled per
-  action through `config::runtime()`.
-- **Keymap.** `keymap.toml` overrides by snake_case action name; the Help overlay is generated from the live map.
-- **Hardware shortcuts** (`␣da ␣dr ␣ia ␣il ␣M`) pre-fill the `:` line with the full virsh command instead of
-  opening bespoke forms: the user sees and edits exactly what runs. Full virsh syntax on `:` always passes through.
-- **Timeouts.** Long virsh jobs get a 24 h limit (others 30 s) and processes are killed on timeout.
-- **Known limitation.** Actions are awaited inside key handling, so a long job (migration, wipe) keeps the UI
-  busy until it finishes. Moving executions to background tasks with progress in the message line is the next
-  structural step.
-
-
-## Disconnection and performance hardening (2026-11-02)
-
-- **Bogus demo data removal when disconnected:** In live mode without `--demo`, if the libvirt connection fails at startup or drops, the dashboard no longer instantiates `DashboardState::demo()`. Instead, `from_summaries(&[])` initializes a clean live state with `connected: false`, preventing fake mock domains, fake host specs, demo Braille charts, and mockup events from appearing.
-- **Empty domain selection handling:** `render_right` and `render_overview` guard against empty domain selections (`sel.name.is_empty()`) when no domains exist or when disconnected, showing clean disconnection notices rather than fabricated demo metrics.
-- **Filter and sort allocations:** `visible_rows()` now borrows names as string slices during sorting instead of cloning `String` on every comparator invocation. Filter queries are lowercased once outside the loop.
-- **Event query search:** `EventsState::visible()` searches event fields directly without allocating intermediate combined strings per event.
-- **Metrics store retains:** Linear O(N*M) retain checks in `MetricsStore::ingest_domains` are replaced with O(N+M) set lookups, and unnecessary clones of previous counters are avoided.
-
-
-## Theming, terminal background, and overlay rendering (2026-11-02)
-
-- **Full-frame background fill:** The root frame draw and individual views now render a background `Block` with `theme.base()` covering the full area, and `panel::block` sets `.style(theme.base())`. Previously, unpainted frame cells (column margins, panel gutters, empty rows below paragraphs and modals) defaulted to `Color::Reset`, which caused transparent gaps in transparent terminals while text elements rendered with opaque background colors.
-- **Truecolor detection and nearest 256-color matching:** `truecolor()` previously only checked `COLORTERM=truecolor|24bit`, which is not set by default on Windows terminals (Windows Terminal, PowerShell, CMD) or terminals setting `TERM_PROGRAM` / 24-bit `TERM`, causing the app to unnecessarily downgrade all themes to xterm-256 indexed colors. Additionally, `xterm256()` previously bypassed the 24 greyscale ramp for non-monochrome RGBs and used rough thresholds, mapping Dracula (`#282a36`) to xterm 17 (VESA navy blue) and Everforest (`#2d353b`) to xterm 23 (VESA teal/green). `truecolor()` now recognizes Windows console subsystem, `WT_SESSION`, `TERM_PROGRAM`, and 24-bit `TERM`, and `xterm256()` implements true Euclidean distance nearest match across the entire 6×6×6 cube and 24 greyscale ramp.
-- **Help modal render ordering:** In `ui::overlays::help`, the outer modal `Block` is rendered before the inner column paragraphs and footer line. When `.style(theme.base())` was added to the block, calling `render_widget(block, modal)` at the end of the function wiped the inner foreground spans back to default text style.
-
-
-## Remote libvirt functionality (2026-11-02)
-
-- **Remote host telemetry without /proc:** When connecting to a remote hypervisor (`!is_local_uri(uri)`), virsh-tui no longer accesses local client `/proc` or `/sys` files. Instead, `virsh nodecpustats --percent` measures remote CPU utilization, and `virsh nodememstats` measures total, free, and available memory in KiB. Per-thread meters, core frequencies, and temperatures are cleanly hidden, displaying remote CPU model and count (`NN% · N CPUs`).
-- **Concurrent host polling:** Because `virsh nodecpustats --percent` blocks 1 second, it is polled concurrently alongside `domains_with_stats()` via `tokio::join!`, ensuring domain statistics are delivered without delay.
-- **Session-based remote domain uptimes:** For remote connections where PID files in `/run/libvirt/qemu/` are inaccessible, the poller tracks when running domains were first observed during the session and displays uptimes prefixed with `≥ ` (e.g. `≥ 5m`, `≥ 1h 20m`), matching `PLAN.md` §4.2.
-- **Dynamic hypervisor hostname and live chrome:** `LIVE` chrome state in `ui::chrome` uses `RwLock` so hostname and refresh interval update dynamically. `virsh hostname` queries the remote hypervisor's hostname at startup and on connection change, displaying the remote hostname across the top bar and views.
-- **Complete `:connect <uri>` lifecycle:** Executing `:connect <uri>` updates URIs across all views (`dash`, `host`, `networks`, `storage`, `events`), re-subscribes the live libvirt event stream (`virsh event --loop`), clears stale domains/selection, and restarts background polling.
-
-## Polkit authentication handling (2026-11-02)
-
-- **Deferred alternate screen and raw mode:** Previously, `enable_raw_mode()` and `EnterAlternateScreen` were called immediately in `main.rs` before `app::run`. When virsh connected to an unauthorized socket (e.g. non-root `qemu:///system`), PolicyKit's textual agent (`pkttyagent`) opened `/dev/tty` while the terminal was already in raw mode. In raw mode, `\n` without `\r` produced staircase formatting, canonical line input/echo was disabled so users could not type responses, and `terminal.clear()` timed out querying the cursor position (`The cursor position could not be read within a normal duration`). Terminal initialization is now managed by an RAII `TerminalGuard` in `app::run` after the initial connection and state preflight, so startup Polkit prompts display with proper line breaks and accept interactive identity and password input.
-- **Detached controlling TTY during active TUI session:** Once the TUI is active, `exec::set_detach_tty(true)` ensures background commands and event streams (in `exec::run`, `exec::run_blocking`, `command::exec::execute`, and `events::stream_once`) run in a new session (`setsid()` on Unix). If permission is denied while the TUI is running or unauthorized, child processes fail immediately with an authentication error without opening `/dev/tty` or corrupting the ratatui interface.
-- **Actionable authentication error messages:** `friendly_first_line` in `exec.rs` recognizes Polkit denial messages (e.g., `authentication unavailable`, `access denied by policy`, `polkit`) and appends `(not in the libvirt group?)`, matching `PLAN.md` §14 error UX.
-
-## Keymap single source of truth (2026-11-03)
-
-- **Unified key binding definitions:** `input::keymap::DEFAULT_BINDINGS` is now the single source of truth for all default key sequences. Changing a key sequence in `DEFAULT_BINDINGS` automatically updates the key engine behavior, the which-key leader popup, the help overlay, and the curated palette shortcuts without needing edits across multiple files.
-- **Dynamic which-key popup:** `ui::widgets::whichkey` was previously hardcoded with static string slices for `"Space"`, `"Space s"`, `"g"`, etc. It now derives its items, sub-prefixes (e.g. `s …`, `m …`), and labels dynamically from the active keymap (`KeyEngine::map()`), respecting user `keymap.toml` overrides and developer binding adjustments while preserving default ordering.
-- **Dynamic help overlay labels:** `ui::overlays::help` previously had disconnected static rows with empty action slices (e.g., `⌫ / q`, `1 … 5`, and static leader titles). All rows are now connected to their corresponding `KeyAction`s and dynamically format bound sequences, multi-key group compacting (`␣s c/r/d`), sequential tab ranges, and dynamic leader prefixes.
-- **Curated command palette synchronization:** Curated palette actions in `ui::overlays::palette::curated_with_map` now resolve their key shortcut strings from the keymap via `input::keymap::action_key_label`, ensuring palette shortcut badges stay in sync.
-
-## Focus movement & tab 3 help (2026-11-04)
-
-- **Focus cycling via `Tab`:** Removed `h` and `l` for focus movement across views and panes. Added `Tab` / `S-Tab` binding mapped to `KeyAction::CycleFocus`. In Networks (tab 3), `l` was removed and `Tab` cycles focus between Networks and DHCP Leases. In Storage (tab 4), `Tab` cycles focus between Pools and Volumes. In Settings, `Tab` / `BackTab` cycles between category and option panes.
-- **Global overlay dispatch in Networks view:** Moved `View::Networks` action handling to the standard match arm after global overlay checks (`Help`, `Palette`, `Settings`, `Ex`), resolving an issue where `?` help was swallowed before reaching the help overlay handler.
diff --git a/docs/DESIGN.md b/docs/DESIGN.md
deleted file mode 100644
index e14828d5b35ee9d720ad5497b5f522afeb48d74d..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
--- a/docs/DESIGN.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,205 +0,0 @@
-# virsh-tui — Design Spec
-
-Mockup sources (exact strings, data, colours): `docs/mockups/*.dc.html`. Implementation plan: `docs/PLAN.md`.
-
-This document is the source of truth for the UI. Every screen on the canvas maps to a section below.
-Stack: Rust + ratatui (+ crossterm). Every effect in the mockups is achievable with per-cell fg/bg/modifiers —
-nothing relies on pixel tricks.
-
----
-
-## 1. Principles
-
-1. **virsh-transparent.** Every action shows the exact `virsh` / `virt-install` command it is about to run
-   (preview before, echo after in the message line). The app teaches virsh while removing the need to memorise it.
-2. **Vim-native.** Modal (NORMAL / INSERT / VISUAL / COMMAND / PALETTE / PICKER / CONFIRM), counts, `.` repeat,
-   `:` ex-commands, `␣` leader with which-key style sub-menus, `gg/G`, `C-d/C-u`, `/` filter, `n/N`.
-3. **Dense but calm.** One accent (blue) for focus; colour carries meaning (state, metric type), never decoration.
-4. **Nothing destructive without a preview.** Destroy / undefine / revert / delete always open a CONFIRM modal with
-   the command list; undefine requires typing the domain name.
-5. **Live.** 1 s default refresh via `virConnectGetAllDomainStats`; libvirt event stream for state changes (no polling for state).
-
----
-
-## 2. Theme tokens
-
-Themes are a flat set of 16 semantic tokens. All widgets use tokens only — never raw colours.
-
-| token     | role                                              | tokyo-night |
-|-----------|---------------------------------------------------|-------------|
-| `bg`      | main background                                   | `#1a1b26` |
-| `bg2`     | top bar, status bar, code blocks, inputs          | `#16161e` |
-| `hl`      | chips, field background, unfocused selection, gauge track | `#292e42` |
-| `sel`     | focused selection row (visual)                    | `#283457` |
-| `gutter`  | unfocused borders, dashed separators              | `#3b4261` |
-| `comment` | labels, hints, dim text, `shut off`               | `#565f89` |
-| `fg`      | primary text                                      | `#c0caf5` |
-| `fg2`     | secondary text, values                            | `#a9b1d6` |
-| `blue`    | focus border, accent, NORMAL mode, active tab     | `#7aa2f7` |
-| `cyan`    | network / IPs / flags in commands / net rx        | `#7dcfff` |
-| `magenta` | memory, snapshots, marks, PALETTE/PICKER mode     | `#bb9af7` |
-| `green`   | running, read I/O, INSERT mode, success, `[x]`    | `#9ece6a` |
-| `yellow`  | paused, warnings, net tx, ISO/media               | `#e0af68` |
-| `orange`  | keys in hints, write I/O, numeric args            | `#ff9e64` |
-| `red`     | crashed, destructive, CONFIRM mode, CPU hot       | `#f7768e` |
-| `teal`    | CPU chart base gradient                           | `#73daca` |
-
-Built-in themes (exact hex values are in every artboard's script, `THEMES` map, key order:
-`bg bg2 hl sel gutter comment fg fg2 blue cyan magenta green yellow orange red teal`):
-
-- `tokyo-night` (**default**), `tokyo-night-storm`, `tokyo-night-day` (light)
-- `catppuccin-mocha`, `gruvbox-dark`, `nord`, `dracula`, `kanagawa`, `everforest`
-
-Custom themes: `~/.config/virsh-tui/themes/<name>.toml` with the same 16 keys. Option `transparent = true`
-renders `bg` as `Color::Reset` (inherit terminal).
-
----
-
-## 3. Global layout (every screen)
-
-```
-┌ row 0  (1 line)  TOP BAR   bg2: [◆ virsh-tui](bg=blue,fg=bg2,bold)  1 Domains  2 Host  3 Networks  4 Storage  5 Events ……  ⌁ uri │ host │ ⟳ 1s │ HH:MM:SS
-│ row 1… (fill)    BODY      panels, 1 cell gap, 1 blank line above first row of panels (room for titles)
-│ row n-1 (1 line) STATUS    bg2: [MODE pill] [breadcrumb (bg=hl)]  key hints (keys orange, text comment) …… [counters (bg=hl)] [extra pill]
-└ row n  (1 line)  MESSAGE   last result: "✓ Started k8s-worker-02  ── virsh start k8s-worker-02" / "-- INSERT --" / errors in red
-```
-
-- **Tabs**: inactive `comment`, number in `orange` bold; active = bg `bg`, fg `blue`, bold.
-- **Mode pill colours**: NORMAL=blue, INSERT=green, VISUAL=magenta, COMMAND=yellow, PALETTE/PICKER=magenta, CONFIRM=red. Text `bg2`, bold.
-- **Message line**: success `green ✓`, error `red ✗`, info `comment`. Always append `── <command>` in `comment` when a virsh call ran.
-- Minimum terminal size: 100×30. Below that, show a centered "terminal too small (WxH, need 100×30)" panel.
-  Layout breakpoints: ≥160 cols → two-column dashboard (as mock); 100–159 → right column moves under the list as tabs (Overview | CPU | Mem | Disk | Net).
-
-### Panel (the basic container)
-
-- `Block::bordered().border_type(Rounded)` (configurable: plain / double / thick).
-- Border `gutter`; **focused** panel border `blue` and title `blue`.
-- Title top-left, bold, `fg2` (padded with one space each side). Optional right title (top-right, `comment`),
-  bottom-left / bottom-right footers in `comment` (sort mode, counts, local key hints).
-- Inner padding: 1 cell horizontal.
-
-### Tables / lists
-
-- Header row: `comment`, bold, underline separator (`hl`).
-- Selected row: bg `sel` (focused panel) or `hl` (unfocused), name bold `fg`, plus a `▌` marker in `blue` in col 0.
-- Marked rows (`m` / VISUAL): `◆` in `magenta` in col 1; status bar shows `N marked` pill (magenta).
-- Row height 1 line (mock uses extra leading only for readability).
-
-### State glyphs (domains)
-
-| state       | glyph | colour   |
-|-------------|-------|----------|
-| running     | `●`   | green    |
-| paused      | `‖`   | yellow   |
-| shut off    | `○`   | comment  |
-| crashed     | `✗`   | red      |
-| pmsuspended | `◌`   | magenta  |
-| in transition (starting/shutting down) | spinner `⠋⠙⠹⠸⠼⠴⠦⠧⠇⠏` | blue |
-
-Icon sets: `unicode` (default, as above), `nerd` (nerd-font glyphs), `ascii` (`* = o x ~`).
-
----
-
-## 4. Charts & gauges (ratatui mapping)
-
-| visual | used in | implementation |
-|--------|---------|----------------|
-| **Braille area chart with vertical gradient** | CPU (dashboard, host) | Custom widget: 2×4 dots per cell (U+2800 + bitmask), filled from the value down. Colour per *row* from a gradient top→bottom: `red, magenta, magenta, blue, blue, cyan, cyan, teal`. Y labels `100% / 50% / 0%` in a 5-col gutter; x labels `-60s -30s now`. |
-| **Mirrored braille** | Network rx/tx | Same widget; rx fills upward (cyan), tx downward (yellow), dashed `gutter` line between. |
-| **Multi-row sparkline** | Memory, Disk R/W | ratatui `Sparkline` (or custom multi-row with `▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█`). Memory = magenta, read = green, write = orange. |
-| **Inline sparkline** | Host "Running domains" table cells, network list | single-row `▁…█` string, coloured by the current level. |
-| **Line gauge** | host CPU/RAM/pools, memory, volume usage | `LineGauge` with `━` filled / `━` in `hl` for the track. Colour by level: `<50% green`, `<80% yellow`, else `red`. |
-| **Eighth-block bar** | CPU% column in domain table | `█` + partial `▏▎▍▌▋▊▉`, track `░` in `hl`, followed by right-aligned `NN%`. |
-| **Per-thread meters** | Host CPU | 32 columns × 3 rows of vertical blocks, row colours `red / blue / cyan`, index under each (comment). |
-| **Stacked bar** | Host memory by domain | full-block segments, one palette colour per domain + legend with `■`. Palette order: orange, blue, magenta, cyan, green, yellow, teal, red, fg2. |
-| **Slider** | wizard / forms | `━━━━●──────` — filled in metric colour, knob bold, track `gutter`. |
-
-Graph style option: `braille` (default) | `block` | `tty` (ASCII). Option `gradient = true|false`.
-History windows: `t` cycles 60 s → 5 min → 1 h (ring buffers per domain per metric; 1 h kept at 10 s resolution).
-
----
-
-## 5. Screens
-
-### 01 · Domains dashboard (`1`)
-- Left column (≈58%): **Domains** table (focus) — columns: marker, mark, state glyph, NAME, STATE, CPU (vCPUs), MEMORY (used/max), CPU% bar, UPTIME, A (autostart ✓/·).
-  Filter bar on top: `/ filter…` + state chips (`all`, `running`, `paused`, `crashed`, `off`) with counts. Footers: `sort: state › name`, `2/15 · 3 marked`.
-- **Events** panel: last 4 libvirt events (`time  glyph  domain  event  detail`), coloured by event type.
-- **Host** panel: 6 line gauges in 2 columns (CPU, RAM, Swap, pools, hugepages).
-- Right column = selected domain: **Overview** (key/value grid + action chips `S r p c v ␣s e`), **CPU** braille chart, **Memory** + **Disk I/O** side by side, **Network** mirrored chart with totals.
-- For shut-off domains, the right column shows config only (no charts) plus a big hint `s to start`.
-
-### 02 · Host monitor (`2`)
-- **CPU** panel: model, freq, temp, load average; 6-row braille history; per-thread meters.
-- **Memory** panel: stacked "host RSS by domain" bar + legend + hugepages / KSM / swap line.
-- **Running domains** table (focus): NAME, vCPU, CPU%, CPU 60 s sparkline, MEM, MEM sparkline, DISK R/W, NET ↓/↑. Title-right: total vCPU / threads and overcommit ratio.
-- Bottom row: **System** (kernel, libvirt, QEMU, KVM/nested/IOMMU, NUMA, uptime), **Storage pools** gauges, **Networks** with sparklines.
-
-### 03 · Domain detail (`⏎` on a domain)
-- Header: breadcrumb `domains › name`, state, uptime, inner tabs **Overview | Monitor | Hardware | Snapshots | Console | XML** (`H/L`).
-- **Hardware**: left **Devices** list (icon coloured by device class, name, summary; `a` add, `d` remove, `J/K` reorder boot), center editor form for the selected device, right **Pending · XML diff** (red `-` / green `+`) and **Will run** (command list, `:w` apply, `u` undo field, `:q!` discard, `gx` open XML).
-- Forms: sections in `blue` bold; fields bg `hl`; focused field bg `sel` + green outline + block cursor in INSERT; radios `(●)/( )`, checkboxes `[x]/[ ]` (green when on); warnings in yellow with `⚠` (e.g. "needs reboot").
-- Every form has an **Apply to** section: `config (--config)` / `live (--live)`.
-- Device editors needed: CPUs (count/max, topology, model, features, pinning, emulatorpin, iothreads), Memory (current/max, balloon, hugepages, shared/virtiofs), Boot (firmware, secure boot, order, menu), Disk (source, bus, cache, io, discard, readonly, size → resize), CDROM (media insert/eject), NIC (source network/bridge, model, MAC, link state, bandwidth), Display (SPICE/VNC, listen, port, password), Video, Sound, Input, TPM, USB redirection / host-device passthrough (USB + PCI).
-- **XML** tab: read-only highlighted XML with folding; `e` opens `$EDITOR` and validates with `virsh define --validate` on save.
-- **Console** tab: instructions + `c` to suspend the TUI and run `virsh console` (Ctrl-] returns), `v` to spawn `virt-viewer`/`remote-viewer` detached.
-
-### 04 · New domain wizard (`␣n`)
-- Centered modal over the dimmed dashboard. Steps: **1 Name & OS → 2 Install media → 3 CPU & Memory → 4 Storage → 5 Network → 6 Review & create**.
-- Left: step list (`✓` done green, `●` current blue on `sel`, `○` todo) with the chosen value under each step; osinfo min/recommended requirements and a check.
-- Right: step form. Sliders + numeric fields; presets as chips (selected chip = magenta bg).
-- Bottom: **Equivalent command** (`virt-install …`) updating live, lines belonging to the current step highlighted with `hl`. `y` copy, `C-e` edit as XML.
-- Keys: `⇥` next field, `h/l` adjust, `H/L` ×step, `C-n/C-p` next/prev step, `⎋` cancel (draft autosaved).
-
-### 05 · Command palette (`C-p`)
-- Modal, top-centered. Input with prefix modes: `❯` actions, `:` ex, `/` domains, `#` docs.
-- Left: fuzzy results (match chars orange bold), icon by category, bound key on the right; then **recent**.
-- Right: **virsh reference** for the highlighted action — SYNOPSIS + OPTIONS (each flag with a `[ ]`/`[x]` toggle via `⇥`) + the resulting command. This is the "never search for the right flag again" feature: the option list is generated from `virsh help <cmd>` (parse at startup, cache).
-- `⏎` opens the action's form pre-filled; `C-y` copies the command.
-
-### 06 · Keybindings (`?`)
-- Full-screen modal, 4 columns of sections (see §6). `/` searches. Destructive actions in red. Footer: counts, `.` repeat, keymap path.
-
-### 07 · Networks (`3`)
-- **Virtual networks** table (name, mode, bridge, subnet, autostart) and **Host interfaces** (iface, type, speed, address, attached vnets).
-- Right: network detail (forward, bridge, IPv4/6, DHCP range, DNS), **Traffic** mirrored chart, **DHCP leases** table (static `◆` magenta / dynamic `●` green) with actions: pin lease as static (`net-update add ip-dhcp-host --live --config`), remove static, copy IP, jump to domain.
-
-### 08 · Storage (`4`)
-- **Pools** (state, type, target path, usage gauge). **Volumes** of the selected pool: NAME, FORMAT, CAPACITY, ALLOC, usage gauge, USED BY (domain, `◆ backing of N` magenta, `⚠ orphan` yellow).
-- Volume actions: `n` new, `R` resize, `C` clone, `u` upload, `W` wipe, `X` delete (confirm).
-- **Insert media picker** (`␣mi`, from any view): fuzzy ISO list from the `isos` pool (or any pool via `⇥`, or filesystem browse), shows current media to be ejected, `live`/`config`/boot-from-cdrom toggles, `virsh change-media … --update --live --config` preview.
-
-### 09 · Snapshots (domain tab)
-- Tree with box-drawing (`├─ │ └─`), `◆` snapshot (magenta), `●` current (green, `← current`), date, state at snapshot, kind (disk / mem+disk).
-- Detail panel: created, state, parent, children, disks, size, description.
-- **CONFIRM modal** (red border, CONFIRM mode): question with names highlighted, consequences in plain words, options (after-revert state, `--force`, "snapshot current state first" ON by default), command list, `n` cancel / `y` revert (red bg).
-
-### 10 · Settings (`,`)
-- Categories: General, Appearance, Keybindings, Connections, Monitoring, Confirmations, Console & viewer.
-- Theme list with 8-colour swatch strip; `j/k` previews **live** (whole app re-themes), `⏎` applies, `⎋` reverts.
-- Appearance options: borders (rounded/plain/double/thick), icons (unicode/nerd/ascii), graphs (braille/block/tty + gradient), transparent background, dim behind modals.
-- Preview panel: 16-token palette + sample rows + gauge + chart.
-- Persisted to `~/.config/virsh-tui/config.toml`.
-
----
-
-## 6. Keymap (default — all remappable in `keymap.toml`)
-
-**Navigation**: `j/k` · `gg/G` · `C-d/C-u` · `Tab` cycle focus · `H/L` prev/next inner tab · `1…5` views · `⏎` open · `⌫`/`q` back · `/` filter · `n/N` next/prev match.
-**Modes**: `i`/`a` edit field (INSERT) · `⎋` NORMAL · `V` visual select · `m` mark · `:` ex · `C-p` palette.
-**Domain**: `s` start · `S` shutdown · `D` destroy● · `r` reboot · `R` reset● · `p` pause/resume · `Z` managed-save · `a` autostart · `c` console · `v` viewer · `e` edit XML · `X` undefine●.
-**Yank**: `yy` name · `yu` uuid · `yi` ip · `yc` last command.
-**Leader `␣`**: `n` new · `c` clone · `r` rename · `M` migrate · `s c/r/d` snapshot new/revert/delete · `mi/me` insert/eject ISO · `da/dr` disk attach/resize · `ia/il` NIC attach/link · `x` export XML · `b` boot order. Pressing `␣` and waiting 300 ms shows a which-key popup bottom-right.
-**Monitor**: `t` window 60s/5m/1h · `+/-` refresh interval · `o` cycle sort · `g c/m/d/n` focus graph.
-**Ex**: `:start <dom>` · `:setmem <dom> 8G --live` · `:attach-iso <dom> <path>` · `:connect <uri>` · `:theme <name>` · `:sort <col>` · `:w` · `:q` · `:qa` · `:!virsh <args>` (raw passthrough, output in a pager).
-**App**: `?` help · `,` settings · `C-r` refresh · `C-l` redraw · `ZZ`/`:qa` quit.
-Counts (`3j`) and `.` (repeat last action on the current/marked selection) work everywhere. Actions on marked domains apply to all marks (bulk).
-(● = confirmation required)
-
----
-
-## 7. Typography & glyphs
-
-- Assumes a monospace font with box-drawing and Braille (U+2800–28FF) coverage (JetBrains Mono / DejaVu Sans Mono / any Nerd Font).
-- Bold only for: titles, selected names, mode pills, keys in hints, active tab.
-- Glyph vocabulary: `◆ ● ○ ‖ ✗ ◌ ▌ ◎ ◫ ▣ ▤ ⏻ ⇄ ▭ ▢ ⌨ ⛨ ⇢ ⌁ ⟳ ❯ ✓ ⚠ ↓ ↑ ━ ─ ░ █ ▁…█ ⠀…⣿`.
